{"abstract":"The COVID-19 pandemic has brought significant and enduring shifts in various aspects of life, including increased flexibility in work arrangements. In a longitudinal study, spanning 24 months with six measurement points from April 2020 to April 2022, we explore changes in well-being, productivity, social contacts, and needs of software engineers during this time. Our findings indicate systematic changes in various variables. For example, well-being and quality of social contacts increased while emotional loneliness decreased as lockdown measures were relaxed. Conversely, people’s boredom and productivity, remained stable. Furthermore, a preliminary investigation into the future of work at the end of the pandemic revealed a consensus among developers for a preference of hybrid work arrangements. We also discovered that prior job changes and low job satisfaction were consistently linked to intentions to change jobs if current work conditions do not meet developers’ needs. This highlights the need for software organizations to adapt to various work arrangements to remain competitive employers. Building upon our findings and the existing literature, we introduce the Integrated Job Demands-Resources and Self-Determination (IJARS) Model as a comprehensive framework to explain the well-being and productivity of software engineers during the COVID-19 pandemic.","author_count":35,"contributors":["Russo, Daniel","Baltes, Sebastian","van Berkel, Niels","Avgeriou, Paris","Calefato, Fabio","Cabrero-Daniel, Beatriz","Catolino, Gemma","Cito, Jürgen","Ernst, Neil","Fritz, Thomas","Hata, Hideaki","Holmes, Reid","Izadi, Maliheh","Khomh, Foutse","Kjærgaard, Mikkel Baun","Liebel, Grischa","Lluch Lafuente, Alberto","Lambiase, Stefano","Maalej, Walid","Murphy, Gail","Moe, Nils Brede","O'Brien, Gabrielle","Paja, Elda","Pezzè, Mauro","Persson, John Stouby","Prikladnicki, Rafael","Ralph, Paul","Robillard, Martin","Silva, Thiago Rocha","Stol, Klaas Jan","Storey, Margaret-Anne","Stray, Viktoria","Tell, Paolo","Treude, Christoph","Vasilescu, Bogdan"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-792887"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["America, North","America, South","Asia, East","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Russo, Daniel"],"country":["Austria","Brazil","Canada","Germany","Iceland","Ireland","Italy","Japan","Netherlands","Norway","Singapore","Sweden","Switzerland","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Carnegie Mellon University","Dalhousie University","Delft University of Technology","McGill University","Polytechnique Montreal","Polytechnique Montréal","Pontifical Catholic University of Rio Grande do Sul","Pontifícia Universidade Católica do Rio Grande do Sul","Reykjavik University","Reykjavík University","SINTEF","SINTEF Industry","Shinshu University","Singapore Management University","TU Wien","USI Università della Svizzera Italiana","University College Cork","University of Bari","University of Bari Aldo Moro","University of Bayreuth","University of British Columbia","University of British Columbia (UBC)","University of Gothenburg","University of Groningen","University of Hamburg","University of Michigan","University of Michigan, Ann Arbor","University of Oslo","University of Salerno","University of Victoria","University of Victoria BC","University of Zurich","University of Zürich","Università della Svizzera italiana","Vienna University of Technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"generative ai in software engineering must be human centered the copenhagen manifesto","src":["aau","dtu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"],"ty