agen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fabio","key":"calefatopau","last":"Calefato","name":"Calefato, Fabio","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Alpana","key":"dubeypau","last":"Dubey","name":"Dubey, Alpana","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Christof","key":"ebertpau","last":"Ebert","name":"Ebert, Christof","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Paolo","key":"tellpau","last":"Tell","locid":"2b8ff3a4-e9b0-403d-8bd8-1bf26121c234","name":"Tell, Paolo","orcid":"0000-0001-7391-0046","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jss.2020.110887","issn":["01641212","18731228"],"issn_org":["01641212"],"journal":"Journal of Systems and Software","pages":"110887","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Systems and Software","volume":"174"},"review":"No Review","scoID":["2-s2.0-85098146835"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ae6ca78d-234c-4509-a086-8932d5e86bb9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Global Software Engineering: Challenges and solutions","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383803","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"When software products and services are developed and maintained over longer time, software engineering practices tend to drift away from both structured and agile methods. Nonetheless, in many cases the evolving practices are far from ad hoc or chaotic. How are the teams involved able to coordinate their joint development?This article reports on an ethnographic study of a small team at a successful provider of software as a service. What struck us was the very explicit way in which the team adopted and adapted their practices to fit the needs of the evolving development. The discussion relates the findings to the concepts of social practices and methods in software engineering, and explores the differences between degraded behavior and the coordinated evolution of development practices. The analysis helps to better understand how software engineering practices evolve, and thus provides a starting point for rethinking software engineering methods and their relation to software engineering practice.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Dittrich, Yvonne","Michelsen, Christian Bo","Tell, Paolo","Lous, Pernille","Ebdrup, Allan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382335"],"event":{"acronym":"ESEC/FSE","title":"ACM Joint European Software Engineering Conference and Symposium on the Foundations of Software Engineering (ESEC/FSE)"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Agile methods","Coordinated development","Ethnographic study","Software as a service","Software engineering practices"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exploring the evolution of software practices","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85597518/FSE2020_Evolving_Practices_author_version_for_the_web.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-382335","identifier":[{"id":"85097200820","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-477045ae-ed39-4b83-9812-da0c73101d14"],"keyword":["Agile methods","Coordinated development","Ethnographic study","Software as a service","Software engineering practices"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EA611A42FF6E64739D329829F76043BE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85597518/FSE2020_Evolving_Practices_author_version_for_the_web.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yvonne","key":"dittrichpau","last":"Dittrich","locid":"f2136570-f73c-446f-9fb0-6d9e461e2124","name":"Dittrich, Yvonne","orcid":"0000-0003-4757-3394","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian Bo","key":"michelsenpau","last":"Michelsen","name":"Michelsen, Christian Bo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Paolo","key":"tellpau","last":"Tell","locid":"2b8ff3a4-e9b0-403d-8bd8-1bf26121c234","name":"Tell, Paolo","orcid":"0000-0001-7391-0046","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pernille","key":"louspau","last":"Lous","name":"Lous, Pernille","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Allan","key":"ebdruppau","last":"Ebdrup","name":"Ebdrup, Allan","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Prem","key":"devanbupedh","last":"Devanbu","name":"Devanbu, Prem","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Myra B.","key":"cohenpedh","last":"Cohen","name":"Cohen, Myra B.","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Thomas","key":"zimmermannpedh","last":"Zimmermann","name":"Zimmermann, Thomas","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3368089.3409766","pages":"493-504","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"ESEC/FSE '20: 28th ACM Joint European Software Engineering Conference and Symposium on the Foundations of Software Engineering, Virtual Event, USA, November 8-13, 2020"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85097200820"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-477045ae-ed39-4b83-9812-da0c73101d14"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Exploring the evolution of software practices","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382335","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Regardless of company size or industry sector, a majority of project teams and companies use customized processes that combine different development methods-so-called hybrid development methods. Even though such hybrid development methods are highly individualized, a common understanding of how to systematically construct synergetic practices is missing. Based on 1,467 data points from a large-scale online survey among practitioners, we study the current state of practice in process use to answer the question: What are hybrid development methods made of? Our findings reveal that only eight methods and few practices build the core of modern software development. This small set allows for statistically constructing hybrid development methods.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Tell, Paolo","Klünder, Jil","Küpper, S.","Raffo, David","MacDonell, Stephen","Münch, Jürgen","Pfahl, D.","Linssen, Oliver","Kuhrmann, Marco"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382657"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Germany","New Zealand"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Auckland University of Technology","FOM University of Applied Sciences","Reutlingen University"],"keyword":["Hybrid Development Methods","Online Survey Analysis","Process Customization","Software Development Practices","Synergetic Practices"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"what are hybrid development methods made of","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18420/SE2020_04","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382657","identifier":[{"id":"85138743729","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-5cb8db6e-1737-456b-961e-15dfb