{"abstract":"Selecting a suitable development method for a specific project context is one of the most challenging activities in process design. Every project is unique and, thus, many context factors have to be considered. Recent research took some initial steps towards statistically constructing hybrid development methods, yet, paid little attention to the peculiarities of context factors influencing method and practice selection. In this paper, we utilize exploratory factor analysis and logistic regression analysis to learn such context factors and to identify methods that are correlated with these factors. Our analysis is based on 829 data points from the HELENA dataset. We provide five base clusters of methods consisting of up to 10 methods that lay the foundation for devising hybrid development methods. The analysis of the five clusters using trained models reveals only a few context factors, e.g., project/product size and target application domain, that seem to significantly influence the selection of methods. An extended descriptive analysis of these practices in the context of the identified method clusters also suggests a consolidation of the relevant practice sets used in specific project contexts.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Klunder, Jil","Karajic, Dzejlana","Tell, Paolo","Karras, Oliver","Munkel, Christian","Munch, Jurgen","MacDonell, Stephen G.","Hebig, Regina","Kuhrmann, Marco"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384795"],"event":{"acronym":"ICSP","title":"International Conference on Software and Systems Process"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Germany","New Zealand","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Auckland University of Technology","Leibniz University Hannover","Reutlingen University","University of Gothenburg","University of Passau"],"keyword":["Context Factors","Development Method Selection","Exploratory factor analysis","Hybrid Development Methods","Logistic Regression Analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"determining context factors for hybrid development methods with trained models","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85582747/2020_03_18_helena_criticality_web.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384795","identifier":[{"id":"85092531702","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-ef9f205d-da32-4d64-a22f-a61164c9b11f"],"keyword":["Context Factors","Development Method Selection","Exploratory Factor Analysis","Hybrid Development Methods","Logistic Regression Analysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-594EADC29DA0BD9365B91C23179F23E1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85582747/2020_03_18_helena_criticality_web.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"leibniz university hannover","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Leibniz University Hannover","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"university of passau","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Passau","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"reutlingen university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Reutlingen University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"nz","key":"auckland university of technology","loc":["New Zealand","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Auckland University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"se","key":"university of gothenburg","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Gothenburg","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jil","key":"klunderpau","last":"Klunder","name":"Klunder, Jil","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Dzejlana","key":"karajicpau","last":"Karajic","name":"Karajic, Dzejlana","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Paolo","key":"tellpau","last":"Tell","locid":"2b8ff3a4-e9b0-403d-8bd8-1bf26121c234","name":"Tell, Paolo","orcid":"0000-0001-7391-0046","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Oliver","key":"karraspau","last":"Karras","name":"Karras, Oliver","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"munkelpau","last":"Munkel","name":"Munkel, Christian","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jurgen","key":"munchpau","last":"Munch","name":"Munch, Jurgen","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Stephen G.","key":"macdonellpau","last":"MacDonell","name":"MacDonell, Stephen G.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Regina","key":"hebigpau","last":"Hebig","name":"Hebig, Regina","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"kuhrmannpau","last":"Kuhrmann","name":"Kuhrmann, Marco","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3379177.3388898","isbn":["9781450375122"],"pages":"61-70","place":"New York, NY, USA","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the International Conference on Software and System Processes"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85092531702"],"search":{