{"abstract":"The first international HELENA workshop was held co-located with the 2017 International Conference on Software and Systems Process (ICSSP). The goals of this workshop were to bring the HELENA team together, foster general networking, discuss the current state of the project, and develop a roadmap towards future activities. From the 84 researchers and practitioners from 25 active countries, 25 participated in this workshop. The overall status report shows that the HELENA survey is increasingly gaining attention, and more then 300 data points have been collected so far. The team agreed on a number of topics for future activities, e.g., organizational transformation, adaptation and evolution, and development approaches for safety-critical systems.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Kuhrmann, Marco","Münch, Jürgen","Tell, Paolo","Diebold, Philipp"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381593"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Clausthal University of Technology","Fraunhofer Institute for Experimental Software Engineering","Reutlingen University"],"keyword":["Agile methods","Hybrid Development Approaches","Process improvement","Software process","process description"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"summary of the 000000000001st international workshop on hybrid development approaches in software systems development","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83523853/2017_07_27HELENA_WS1_Summary_auhtorweb.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381593","ids":["itu-15511540-0b44-4691-87be-ddd765ee6d6d"],"keyword":["agile methods","hybrid development approaches","process description","process improvement","software process"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-CC6F49199EDF4BEBEBB4D26249888AAB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83523853/2017_07_27HELENA_WS1_Summary_auhtorweb.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"clausthal university of technology","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Clausthal University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"reutlingen university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Reutlingen University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"fraunhofer institute for experimental software engineering","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Fraunhofer Institute for Experimental Software Engineering","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"kuhrmannpau","last":"Kuhrmann","name":"Kuhrmann, Marco","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jürgen","key":"münchpau","last":"Münch","name":"Münch, Jürgen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Paolo","key":"tellpau","last":"Tell","locid":"2b8ff3a4-e9b0-403d-8bd8-1bf26121c234","name":"Tell, Paolo","orcid":"0000-0001-7391-0046","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Philipp","key":"dieboldpau","last":"Diebold","name":"Diebold, Philipp","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3149485.3149519","issn":["01635948","19435843"],"issn_org":["01635948"],"issue":"4","journal":"Software Engineering Notes","pages":"18-20","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Software Engineering Notes","title_org":"SIGSOFT Software Engineering Notes","volume":"42"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-15511540-0b44-4691-87be-ddd765ee6d6d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Summary of the 1st International Workshop on Hybrid Development Approaches in Software Systems Development","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381593","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Since the early days of software engineering, a number of methods, processes, and practices to design and develop software systems have been proposed and applied in industry, e.g., the Rational Unified Process, Agile Software Development, etc. However, since no silver bullet exists, organizations use rich combinations of agile and/or traditional methods and practices, rather than following a single process by the book. To investigate this reality, an international exploratory multistage research project named HELENA (Hybrid DEveLopmENt Approaches in software systems development) was initiated. Currently, the HELENA survey is conducted globally (second stage of HELENA project). This short paper presents and discusses the results of the survey in Danmark compared to the global results based on the data from August 15, 2017.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Tell, Paolo","Pfeiffer, Rolf Helge","Schultz, Ulrik Pagh"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-624700"],"event":{"acronym":"PROFES","end":"2017-12-01","place":"Innsbruck, at","start":"2017-11-29","title":"18th International Conference on Product-Focused Software Process Improvement, PROFES 2017","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Tell, Paolo"],"keyword":["Helena","Hybrid Development Approaches"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-BA","DI-U"],"level3":{"BA":["DI-BA-ALL","DI-BA-CBA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-BA-CBA","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"helena stage 000000000002 danish overview","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85034568931","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-624700","identifier":[{"id":"85034568931","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-b3c3eaba-3298-4a38-afb1-3cc86d9e1649"],"keyword":["HELENA","Hybrid development approaches"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-255944DCDE5032D8912852992CA57E95"],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"cphbusiness copenhagen business academy","l2":"DI-BA","l2n":"Business Academies","l3":"DI-BA-CBA","l3nn":"CPHBusiness - Copenhagen Business Academy","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CPHBusiness - Copenhagen Business Academy","namevar":["Copenhagen Business Academy"],"nora_code":"DI-BA-CBA","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, The Maersk Mc-Kinney Moller Institute","SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, The Maersk Mc-Kinney Moller Institute, SDU Software Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Paolo","key":"tellpau","last":"Tell","name":"Tell, Paolo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rolf Helge","key":"pfeifferpau","last":"Pfeiffer","name":"Pfeiffer, Rolf Helge","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ulrik Pagh","key":"schultzpau","last":"Schultz","locid":"79a07bec-ac88-404c-8d6b-c9180214bcc6","name":"Schultz, Ulrik Pagh","orcid":"0000-0003-4119-2689","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael","key":"feldererpedh","last":"Felderer","name":"Felderer, Michael","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Daniel","key":"méndezfernándezpedh","last":"Méndez Fernández","name":"Méndez Fernández, Daniel","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Burak","key":"turhanpedh","last":"Turhan","name":"Turhan, Burak","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Marcos","key":"kalinowskipedh","last":"Kalinowski","name":"Kalinowski, Marcos","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Federica","key":"sarropedh","last":"Sarro","name":"Sarro, Federica","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Dietmar","key":"winklerpedh","last":"Winkler","name":"Winkler, Dietmar","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-69926-4_31","eisbn":["9783319699264"],"isbn":["9783319699257"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"420-427","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"18th International Conference, PROFES 2017, Innsbruck, Austria, November 29–December 1, 2017, Proceedings","title":"Product-Focused Software Process Improvement"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85034568931"],"search":{"DAF":["All Business Academies","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Business Academies","DI-ALL","DI-BA","DI-BA-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-b3c3eaba-3298-4a38-afb1-3cc86d9e1649"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"HELENA stage 2—danish overview","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-624700","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Distributed software engineering and agility are strongly pushing on today's software industry. Due to inherent incompatibilities, for years, studying Scrum and its application in distributed setups has been subject to theoretical and applied research, and an increasing body of knowledge reports insights into this combination. Through a systematic literature review, this paper contributes a collection of experiences on the application of Scrum to global software engineering (GSE). In total, we identified 40 challenges in 19 categories practitioners face when using Scrum in GSE. Among the challenges, scaling Scrum to GSE and adopting practices accordingly are the most frequently named. Our findings also show that most solution proposals aim at modifying elements of the Scrum core processes. We thus conclude that, even though Scrum allows for extensive modification, Scrum itself represents a barrier for global software engineering, and development teams have to customize Scrum properly to benefit from agile software development in GSE.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Lous, Pernille","Kuhrmann, Marco","Tell, Paolo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382248"],"event":{"acronym":"ICGSE","title":"IEEE/ACM International Conference on Global Software Engineering"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Clausthal University of Technology"],"keyword":["Agility","Distributed Software Engineering","Global Software Engineering","Scrum","Systematic literature review"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"is scrum fit for global software engineering","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82295258/PID4666577_Preprint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382248","identifier":[{"id":"85027714719","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-42207f34-b003-407e-9729-d4d5ec0ce2b5"],"keyword":["Agility","Distributed Software Engineering","Global Software Engineering","Scrum","Systematic Literature Review"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A4BFC2AE2B7845D662E0D62848BA3372"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82295258/PID4666577_Preprint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"clausthal university of technology","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Clausthal University of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pernille","key":"louspau","last":"Lous","name":"Lous, Pernille","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"kuhrmannpau","last":"Kuhrmann","name":"Kuhrmann, Marco","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Paolo","key":"tellpau","last":"Tell","locid":"2b8ff3a4-e9b0-403d-8bd8-1bf26121c234","name":"Tell, Paolo","orcid":"0000-0001-7391-0046","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/icgse.2017.13","eisbn":["9781538615874"],"publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Global Software Engineering (ICGSE), 2017 IEEE 12th International Conference on"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85027714719"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-42207f34-b003-407e-9729-d4d5ec0ce2b5"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Is Scrum fit for global software engineering?","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382248","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Software and system development faces numerous challenges of rapidly changing markets. To address such challenges, companies and projects design and adopt specific development approaches by combining well-structured comprehensive methods and flexible agile practices. Yet, the number of methods and practices is large, and available studies argue that the actual process composition is carried out in a fairly ad-hoc manner. The present paper reports on a survey on hybrid software development approaches. We study which approaches are used in practice, how different approaches are combined, and what contextual factors influence the use and combination of hybrid software development approaches. Our results from 69 study participants show a variety of development approaches used and combined in practice. We show that most combinations follow a pattern in which a traditional process model serves as framework in which several fine-grained (agile) practices are plugged in. We further show that hybrid software development approaches are independent from the company size and external triggers. We conclude that such approaches are the results of a natural process evolution, which is mainly driven by experience, learning, and pragmatism.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Kuhrmann, Marco","Diebold, Philipp","Münch, Jürgen","Tell, Paolo","Garousi, Vahid","Felderer, Michael","Trektere, Kitija","McCaffery, Fergal","Linssen, Oliver","Hanser, Eckhart","Prause, Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381444"],"event":{"acronym":"ICSP","title":"International Conference on Software and Systems Process"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Austria","Germany","Ireland","Luxembourg"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Clausthal University of Technology","Dundalk Institute of Technology","FOM University of Applied Sciences","Fraunhofer Institute for Experimental Software Engineering","German Aerospace Center","Reutlingen University","University of Applied Sciences Baden-Württemberg Lörrach","University of Innsbruck","University of Luxembourg"],"keyword":["Agile software development","Hybrid Development Approaches","Software process","Survey"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hybrid software and system development in practice waterfall scrum and beyond","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82295280/helena1_icssp_web_1_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381444","identifier":[{"id":"85025802609","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-0c5727b1-efbd-4d13-8601-9242c96a06fd"],"keyword":["Agile software development","hybrid development approaches","software process","survey"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7FAD5985C3A6F1887C1742BB59FB8568"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82295280/helena1_icssp_web_1_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"clausthal university of technology","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Clausthal University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"fraunhofer institute for experimental software engineering","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Fraunhofer Institute for Experimental Software Engineering","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"reutlingen university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Reutlingen University","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"lu","key":"university of luxembourg","loc":["Luxembourg","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Luxembourg","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"at","key":"university of innsbruck","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Innsbruck","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"ie","key":"dundalk institute of technology","loc":["Ireland","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Dundalk Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"de","key":"fom university of applied sciences","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"FOM University of Applied Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"9","country":"de","key":"university of applied sciences baden württemberg lörrach","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Applied Sciences Baden-Württemberg Lörrach","used":1},{"affno":"10","country":"de","key":"german aerospace center","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"German Aerospace Center","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"kuhrmannpau","last":"Kuhrmann","name":"Kuhrmann, Marco","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Philipp","key":"dieboldpau","last":"Diebold","name":"Diebold, Philipp","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jürgen","key":"münchpau","last":"Münch","name":"Münch, Jürgen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Paolo","key":"tellpau","last":"Tell","locid":"2b8ff3a4-e9b0-403d-8bd8-1bf26121c234","name":"Tell, Paolo","orcid":"0000-0001-7391-0046","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Vahid","key":"garousipau","last":"Garousi","name":"Garousi, Vahid","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"feldererpau","last":"Felderer","name":"Felderer, Michael","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Kitija","key":"trekterepau","last":"Trektere","name":"Trektere, Kitija","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Fergal","key":"mccafferypau","last":"McCaffery","name":"McCaffery, Fergal","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","corresponding":null,"first":"Oliver","key":"linssenpau","last":"Linssen","name":"Linssen, Oliver","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9","corresponding":null,"first":"Eckhart","key":"hanserpau","last":"Hanser","name":"Hanser, Eckhart","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"10","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"prausepau","last":"Prause","name":"Prause, Christian","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3084100.3084104","isbn":["9781450352703"],"pages":"30-39","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"ICSSP 2017","title":"Proceedings of the 2017 International Conference on Software and System Process"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85025802609"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-0c5727b1-efbd-4d13-8601-9242c96a06fd"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Hybrid Software and System Development in Practice: Waterfall, Scrum, and Beyond","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381444","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Since the early days of software engineering, a number of methods, processes, and practices to design and develop software systems have been proposed and applied in industry, e.g., the Rational Unified Process, Agile Software Development, etc. However, since no silver bullet exists, organizations use rich combinations of agile and/or traditional methods and practices, rather than following a single process by the book. To investigate this reality, an international exploratory multistage research project named HELENA (Hybrid DEveLopmENt Approaches in software systems development) was initiated. Currently, the HELENA survey is conducted globally (second stage of HELENA project). This short paper presents and discusses the results of the survey in Danmark compared to the global results based on the data from August 15, 2017.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Tell, Paolo","Pfeiffer, Rolf-Helge","Pagh Schultz, Ulrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381708"],"event":{"acronym":"PROFES","title":"International Conference on Product-Focused Software Process Improvement"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Agile software development","HELENA Project","Hybrid Development Approaches","Software Development Practices","Traditional Software Engineering Methods"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-BA","DI-U"],"level3":{"BA":["DI-BA-ALL","DI-BA-CBA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-BA-CBA","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"helena stage 000000000002 danish overview","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82348245/WRKSHP_03_WEB_Tell_etal.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381708","identifier":[{"id":"85034568931","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-1db17eca-2766-43d3-8668-6d8f8130c1b0"],"keyword":["Agile Software Development","HELENA Project","Hybrid Development Approaches","Software Development Practices","Traditional Software Engineering Methods"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-255944DCDE5032D8912852992CA57E95"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82348245/WRKSHP_03_WEB_Tell_etal.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"cphbusiness copenhagen business academy","l2":"DI-BA","l2n":"Business Academies","l3":"DI-BA-CBA","l3nn":"CPHBusiness - Copenhagen Business Academy","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CPHBusiness - Copenhagen Business Academy","namevar":["Copenhagen Business Academy"],"nora_code":"DI-BA-CBA","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Paolo","key":"tellpau","last":"Tell","locid":"2b8ff3a4-e9b0-403d-8bd8-1bf26121c234","name":"Tell, Paolo","orcid":"0000-0001-7391-0046","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rolf-Helge","key":"pfeifferpau","last":"Pfeiffer","name":"Pfeiffer, Rolf-Helge","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulrik","key":"paghschultzpau","last":"Pagh Schultz","name":"Pagh Schultz, Ulrik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-69926-4_31","eisbn":["9783319699264"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"420","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"HELENA – 2nd Workshop on Hybrid Software and System Development Approaches","title":"International Conference on Product-Focused Software Process Improvement - PROFES 2017"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85034568931"],"search":{"DAF":["All Business Academies","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Business Academies","DI-ALL","DI-BA","DI-BA-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1db17eca-2766-43d3-8668-6d8f8130c1b0"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"HELENA Stage 2—Danish Overview","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381708","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Objective: Even though a number of tools is reported to be used by researchers undertaking systematic reviews, important shortages are still reported revealing how such solutions are unable to satisfy current needs. Method: Two researchers independently provided a competing design for a tool supporting systematic reviews. The resulting tools were assessed against the feature lists provided by prior research. Results: After presenting an overview of the tools and the core design decisions taken, we provide a feature analysis and a discussion regarding selected challenges deemed crucial to provide a proper tool support. Conclusions: Although the designed solutions do not yet support the entire systematic review process, their architecture has been designed to be flexible and extendable. After highlighting the difficulties of developing appropriate tools, we call for action: developing tools to support systematic reviews is a community project.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Tell, Paolo","Cholewa, Jacob","Kuhrmann, Marco","Nellemann, Peter"],"cuid":["S02-098.72-038341"],"event":{"end":"2016-06-03","place":"Limerick, ie","start":"2016-06-01","title":"20th International Conference on Evaluation and Assessment in Software Engineering","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Design Exploration","Literature study","Prototyping","TOOL"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"beyond the spreadsheet reflections on tool support for literature studies","src":["itu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/120485844/paper_web.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-098.72-038341","identifier":[{"id":"84978484185","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-83cb8e3b-fa90-415a-a23e-5cfce8801deb","sdu-e128b0ec-996a-4bac-9d33-acb7539db52a"],"keyword":["design exploration","literature study","prototyping","tool"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-C863ADFA2EED2CF3DC7290D10AB426E5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/120485844/paper_web.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/301287807_Beyond_the_Spreadsheet_Reflections_on_Tool_Support_for_Literature_Studies","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, The Maersk Mc-Kinney Moller Institute","SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, The Maersk Mc-Kinney Moller Institute, SDU Software Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Paolo","key":"tellpau","last":"Tell","locid":"2b8ff3a4-e9b0-403d-8bd8-1bf26121c234","name":"Tell, Paolo","orcid":"0000-0001-7391-0046","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob Benjamin","key":"cholewapau","last":"Cholewa","name":"Cholewa, Jacob Benjamin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"kuhrmannpau","last":"Kuhrmann","locid":"4c2b70f1-7dec-456c-939d-81fc0e611fbc","name":"Kuhrmann, Marco","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"nellemannpau","last":"Nellemann","locid":"6dfae08a-ea93-4e13-a75b-3ced8cb511e8","name":"Nellemann, Peter","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2915970.2916011","isbn":["9781450336918"],"publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"EASE '16 Proceedings of the 20th International Conference on Evaluation and Assessment in Software Engineering"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84978484185"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-83cb8e3b-fa90-415a-a23e-5cfce8801deb","sdu-e128b0ec-996a-4bac-9d33-acb7539db52a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Beyond the Spreadsheet : Reflections on Tool Support for Literature Studies","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.72-038341","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Software engineering (SE) is predominantly a team effort that needs close cooperation among several people who may be geographically distributed. It has been recognized that appropriate tool support is a prerequisite to improve cooperation within SE teams. In an effort to contribute to this line of research, we have designed and developed an infrastructure, called ABC4GSD, based on the models of activity theory (AT) and the principles of the activity-based computing (ABC) paradigm. In this paper, we present a study that empirically evaluates the ability of ABC4GSD in supporting teams cooperation. We designed and executed a study based on a scenario that simulated the follow-the-Sun (FTS) strategy of global SE (GSE). Our research design allowed us to ensure cooperation to be both computer-mediated as well as contained within observable short time-windows - the hand-off activities of the FTS strategy. [Results] Overall, the results show that the cooperation support provided by the ABC4GSD system has been positively perceived by the participants. Nonetheless, open issues stimulating further investigations have been raised especially due to a few mixed results. Aware of the limitations of the simulated scenario, we conclude that the approach followed by the ABC4GSD system based on activities is desirable to improve the cooperation support in SE. Finally, our research approach based on simulating a scenario with geographical and temporal distribution can provide useful ideas for assessing collaborative technologies in SE.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Tell, Paolo","Babar, Muhammad Ali"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383234"],"event":{"acronym":"ICGSE","title":"IEEE/ACM International Conference on Global Software Engineering"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Activity theory","Geographically Distributed Teams","Global Software Development","Software Engineering","Team Cooperation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an empirical evaluation of an activity based infrastructure for supporting cooperation in software engineering","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82478873/ICGSE_16_CR.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383234","identifier":[{"id":"84994619251","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-85b278c6-b82c-401b-8019-cb36f09485a8"],"keyword":["Activity Theory","Geographically Distributed Teams","Global Software Development","Software Engineering","Team Cooperation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-352DFA7EF9AC06054E3F7ADB12186F1F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82478873/ICGSE_16_CR.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Paolo","key":"tellpau","last":"Tell","locid":"2b8ff3a4-e9b0-403d-8bd8-1bf26121c234","name":"Tell, Paolo","orcid":"0000-0001-7391-0046","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Muhammad Ali","key":"babarpau","last":"Babar","name":"Babar, Muhammad Ali","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/icgse.2016.25","eisbn":["9781509026807"],"pages":"34-43","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Global Software Engineering (ICGSE), 2016 IEEE 11th International Conference on"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84994619251"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-85b278c6-b82c-401b-8019-cb36f09485a8"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"An Empirical Evaluation of an Activity-Based Infrastructure for Supporting Cooperation in Software Engineering","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383234","year":"2016","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"In this paper, we describe the interaction design and implementation of co-Laevo: an activity-centric desktop computing system supporting task coordination within cooperating teams. Coordination is supported by having all team members orchestrate their dependent tasks on a shared activity time line. Each task (or activity) is associated with a personal dedicated workspace within which related resources, like files and windows, are embedded. As users access activity workspaces, the past, current, and planned state of the activity can be updated to reflect ongoing work. In contrast to stand-alone scheduling tools, like a team calendar, the actual work is not disconnected from the plan. In essence, users work ‘within’ a shared schedule, suspending and resuming activity workspaces in order to access the contained resources required for their work. Users are thereby constantly confronted with their own and collaborators’ activities as part of task switching during everyday work. We introduce this concept, and several entailing design implications, as cooperative activity life cycle management. We anticipate the design of such a system to decrease information overload and increases awareness among team members.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Jeuris, Steven","Tell, Paolo","Bardram, Jakob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383779"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Activity Centric Computing","Interaction design","Task coordination","Team collaboration","Workspace management"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"co laevo supporting cooperating teams by working within shared activity time lines","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81034318/ITU_TR_2016_193.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383779","ids":["itu-ad1f6194-1116-4217-9adc-3ce21df3829f"],"keyword":["Activity-centric computing","Interaction design","Task coordination","Team collaboration","Workspace management"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-5AD09159668A2A4F2FB4290113686D1C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81034318/ITU_TR_2016_193.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Steven","key":"jeurispau","last":"Jeuris","name":"Jeuris, Steven","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Paolo","key":"tellpau","last":"Tell","locid":"2b8ff3a4-e9b0-403d-8bd8-1bf26121c234","name":"Tell, Paolo","orcid":"0000-0001-7391-0046","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob","key":"bardrampau","last":"Bardram","name":"Bardram, Jakob","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["16006100"],"issue":"TR-2016-193","pages":"14","place":"Copenhagen","publisher":"IT-Universitetet i København","repno":"IT University Technical Report Series, TR-2016-193","series":"IT University Technical Report Series","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ad1f6194-1116-4217-9adc-3ce21df3829f"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"co-Laevo - Supporting Cooperating Teams by Working 'within' Shared Activity Time Lines","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383779","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"For decades, Software Process Improvement (SPI) programs have been implemented, inter alia, to improve quality and speed of software development. To set up, guide, and carry out SPI projects, and to measure SPI state, impact, and success, a multitude of different SPI approaches and considerable experience are available. SPI addresses many aspects ranging from individual developer skills to entire organizations. It comprises for instance the optimization of specific activities in the software lifecycle as well as the creation of organization awareness and project culture. In the course of conducting a systematic mapping study on the state-of-the-art in SPI from a general perspective, we observed Global Software Engineering (GSE) becoming a topic of interest in recent years. Therefore, in this paper, we provide a detailed investigation of those papers from the overall systematic mapping study that were classified as addressing SPI in the context of GSE. From the main study’s result set, a set of 30 papers dealing with GSE was selected for an in-depth analysis using the systematic review instrument to study the contributions and to develop an initial picture of how GSE is considered from the perspective of SPI. Our findings show the analyzed papers delivering a substantial discussion of cultural models and how such models can be used to better address and align SPI programs with multi-national environments. Furthermore, experience is shared discussing how agile approaches can be implemented in companies working at the global scale. Finally, success factors and barriers are studied to help companies implementing SPI in a GSE context.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Kuhrmann, Marco","Diebold, Philipp","Münch, Jürgen","Tell, Paolo"],"cuid":["S02-091.38-038365"],"event":{"acronym":"ICGSE","end":"2016-08-05","place":"Irvine, Orange County, California, us","start":"2016-08-02","title":"IEEE/ACM International Conference on Global Software Engineering","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Fraunhofer Institute for Experimental Software Engineering","Reutlingen University"],"keyword":["Agile methodologies","Cultural Models","Global Software Development","Global Software Engineering","Software process improvement","Success Factors and Barriers","Systematic literature review","Systematic mapping study"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how does software process improvement address global software engineering","src":["itu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/121085567/spi_gse_web.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-091.38-038365","identifier":[{"id":"84994644499","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-b3a77171-fdb9-4ee8-a8a7-d84341dd6a42","sdu-91483365-6184-4129-a2da-e825733b2a71"],"keyword":["Agile Methodologies","Cultural Models","Global Software Engineering","Success Factors and Barriers","global software development","software process improvement","systematic literature review","systematic mapping study"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-816335B105C890B3F50EB5E6ACCCB1BA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82478879/spi_gse_web_1_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/121085567/spi_gse_web.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, The Maersk Mc-Kinney Moller Institute, SDU Software Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"fraunhofer institute for experimental software engineering","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Fraunhofer Institute for Experimental Software Engineering","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"reutlingen university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Reutlingen University","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"kuhrmannpau","last":"Kuhrmann","locid":"4c2b70f1-7dec-456c-939d-81fc0e611fbc","name":"Kuhrmann, Marco","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Philipp","key":"dieboldpau","last":"Diebold","name":"Diebold, Philipp","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jürgen","key":"münchpau","last":"Münch","name":"Münch, Jürgen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Paolo","key":"tellpau","last":"Tell","locid":"2b8ff3a4-e9b0-403d-8bd8-1bf26121c234","name":"Tell, Paolo","orcid":"0000-0001-7391-0046","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/icgse.2016.10","eisbn":["9781509026807"],"isbn":["9781509026814"],"pages":"89-98","publisher":"IEEE Press","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 11th IEEE International Conference on Global Software Engineering"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84994644499"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b3a77171-fdb9-4ee8-a8a7-d84341dd6a42","sdu-91483365-6184-4129-a2da-e825733b2a71"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"How Does Software Process Improvement Address Global Software Engineering?","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-091.38-038365","year":"2016","yearsub":2017}
{"abstract":"In this paper we present the dBoard - a digital Scrum Board for distributed Agile software development teams. The dBoard is designed as a 'virtual window' between two Scrum team spaces. It connects two locations with live video and audio, which is overlaid with a synchronized and interactive digital Scrum board, and it adapts the fidelity of the video/audio to the presence of people in front of it. The dBoard is designed to work (i) as a passive information radiator from which it is easy to get an overview of the status of work, (ii) as a media space providing awareness about the presence of remote co-workers, and (iii) as an active meeting support tool. The paper presents a case study of distributed Scrum in a large software company that motivates the design of the dBoard, and details the design and technical implementation of the dBoard. The paper also reports on an initial user study, which shows that users found the dBoard both useful and easy to use. Based on this work, we suggest that superimposing collaborative applications onto live video is a useful way of designing collaborative meeting and awareness systems.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Esbensen, Morten","Tell, Paolo","Cholewa, Jacob Benjamin","Pedersen, Mathias Kindsholm","Bardram, Jakob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382580"],"event":{"acronym":"ISS","title":"ACM International Conference on Interactive Surfaces and Spaces"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Digital Collaboration","Distributed Agile","Media Space","Scrum Board","User study"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the dboard a digital scrum board for distributed software development","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"acces