{"abstract":"Assessing the presence and availability of a remote colleague is key in coordination in global software development but is not easily done using existing computer-mediated channels. Previous research has shown that automated estimation of interruptibility is feasible and can achieve a precision closer to, or even better than, human judgment. However, existing approaches to assess interruptibility have been designed to rely on external sensors. In this paper, we present Approximator, a system that estimates the interruptibility of a user based exclusively on the sensing ability of commodity laptops. Experimental results show that the information aggregated from several activity monitors (i.e., Key-logger, mouse-logger, and face-detection) provide useful data, which, once combined with machine learning techniques, can automatically estimate the interruptibility of users with a 78% accuracy. These early but promising results represent a starting point for designing tools with support for interruptibility capable of improving distributed awareness and cooperation to be used in global software development.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Tell, Paolo","Jalaliniya, Shahram","Andersen, Kristian S. M.","Christensen, Mads D.","Mellson, Anders B.","Bardram, Jakob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382731"],"event":{"acronym":"ICGSE","title":"IEEE/ACM International Conference on Global Software Engineering"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Computer mediated communication","Global Software Development","Interruptibility Estimation","Machine learning","Remote collaboration"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"approximator predicting interruptibility in software development with commodity computers","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://ieeexplore.ieee.org/xpl/articleDetails.jsp?arnumber=7224485","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382731","identifier":[{"id":"84957927531","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-61a083fc-3fba-4746-91c7-dabd56178a1f"],"keyword":["Computer-Mediated Communication","Global Software Development","Interruptibility Estimation","Machine Learning","Remote Collaboration"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-907241058A9928FECB15D4AD9C05F5B3"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Paolo","key":"tellpau","last":"Tell","locid":"2b8ff3a4-e9b0-403d-8bd8-1bf26121c234","name":"Tell, Paolo","orcid":"0000-0001-7391-0046","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shahram","key":"jalaliniyapau","last":"Jalaliniya","name":"Jalaliniya, Shahram","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristian S. M.","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Kristian S. M.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mads D.","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Mads D.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders B.","key":"mellsonpau","last":"Mellson","name":"Mellson, Anders B.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob","key":"bardrampau","last":"Bardram","name":"Bardram, Jakob","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9781479984091"],"pages":"90-99","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"10th International Conference on Global Software Engineering (ICGSE) 2015"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84957927531"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-61a083fc-3fba-4746-91c7-dabd56178a1f"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Approximator: Predicting Interruptibility in Software Development with Commodity Computers","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382731","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
